invariant: INV-69
file: src/mlkem_neon.c
catches: keccak_neon_equiv_test
reason: the ML-KEM sampler hands each state the indices of A where the caller
  asks for A^T, so encryption multiplies by the wrong matrix. The
  equivalence test compares each entry with mlk_sample_ntt's for both
  transposes.

--- old
        x0[k] = transposed ? (uint8_t)i : (uint8_t)(first + k);
        x1[k] = transposed ? (uint8_t)(first + k) : (uint8_t)i;
--- new
        x0[k] = (uint8_t)(first + k + 0U * (unsigned)transposed);
        x1[k] = (uint8_t)i;
